Deliberately NOT distributed here
---------------------------------

The author's private working corpus uses two further witnesses:

    殆知阁古代文献  儒藏/礼经/周礼.txt        (白文, simplified)
    殆知阁古代文献  儒藏/礼经/周礼注疏.txt     (鄭玄注/賈公彥疏, simplified)

Their upstream repository, https://github.com/garychowcmu/daizhigev20 ,
declares **no license**. Nothing from those files — neither the text nor any
collation derived from them — is redistributed in this repository.

`scripts/fetch_corpus.py --with-daizhige` can retrieve them for local, private
use if you want the fuller collation. Fetching them is your own decision and
your own responsibility; if you publish results built on them, the licensing
question is yours to resolve, not this project's.

Note also that the 白文 witness carries a number of clear transcription errors
(for example 建宫以捂 for 建國辨方, 疱人 for 庖人, 胥信人 for 胥十有二人).
It is useful for collation precisely because it disagrees; it is not a text to
cite on its own authority.


